@using System.Globalization
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Localization.IStringLocalizer<SharedResources> L
@inject TimeProvider Clock
@* The brand panel beside the sign-in form on wide viewports. Everything in it is decoration or
   brand copy, so at narrower widths the stylesheet drops the whole aside rather than reflowing
   it — there is nothing here a user needs to complete the task. *@
@* Hidden from assistive technology in its entirety. It is brand decoration that sits before
   the form in reading order, so announcing a wordmark, a tagline, a marketing sentence and a
   copyright notice would cost a screen-reader user all of that on every visit to a page whose
   whole purpose is a two-field form. Nothing here is an instruction, a control, or anything
   the form cannot be completed without, and the product name is already in the document
   title. Safe to hide because it contains nothing focusable — aria-hidden over a focusable
   element strands a keyboard user on a control their screen reader cannot see. *@
<aside class="tmi-ink" aria-hidden="true">
    @* Coloured by class, never by presentation attribute: a fill="" cannot take a var(), and the
       stylesheet is meant to be the only place a colour is decided.

       This one is scaled to cover the panel and cropped to fit, which is right for a field of
       stars — there is no part of it that has to survive. *@
    <svg class="tmi-ink-art" viewBox="0 0 400 600" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
         aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <ellipse class="tmi-ink-orbit" cx="200" cy="300" rx="330" ry="185" transform="rotate(-25 200 300)" />
        <g class="tmi-ink-stars">
            <circle cx="60" cy="90" r="1.4" /><circle cx="150" cy="50" r="1" />
            <circle cx="330" cy="80" r="1.6" /><circle cx="380" cy="180" r="1.1" />
            <circle cx="90" cy="260" r="1.3" /><circle cx="40" cy="430" r="1.5" />
            <circle cx="200" cy="470" r="1" /><circle cx="330" cy="430" r="1.4" />
            <circle cx="160" cy="560" r="1.2" />
        </g>
    </svg>

    @* The comet is its own element, placed against the panel's top corner at a fixed size, and
       deliberately not part of the drawing above. A covering fill crops whichever axis is
       over-long — width on a tall monitor, height on a short one — and the comet sits near a
       corner, so it is the first thing lost either way. Nothing here is cropped by anything.
       Scaled and faded rather than animating the r attribute the mockup uses: r as a
       CSS-animatable geometry property has the thinnest engine support in this design. *@
    <svg class="tmi-ink-comet-art" viewBox="0 0 130 180" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <g class="tmi-ink-trail">
            <circle cx="46" cy="52" r="4" /><circle cx="72" cy="86" r="3.2" />
            <circle cx="94" cy="118" r="2.5" /><circle cx="112" cy="148" r="1.9" />
            <circle cx="128" cy="178" r="1.4" />
        </g>
        @* The head sits far enough inside the viewBox for its halo to breathe: an <svg> clips at
           its viewport, and the halo pulses to 1.19 x its 13 radius, so anything closer than
           ~16 to an edge loses a sliver at the top of every cycle. Keep cx and cy above that
           if either the radius or the keyframe's scale changes. *@
        <circle class="tmi-ink-halo" cx="18" cy="22" r="13" />
        <circle class="tmi-ink-comet" cx="18" cy="22" r="7" />
    </svg>

    <div class="tmi-ink-stack">
        <partial name="/Areas/Identity/Pages/Shared/_Wordmark.cshtml" model="true" />
        <p class="tmi-ink-tagline">@L["BrandTagline"]</p>
        <p class="tmi-ink-blurb">@L["BrandBlurb"]</p>
        @* The year comes from the clock, so a notice that is wrong the moment it ships cannot be
           left behind in a resource file. Passed as text: an ICU argument given a number is
           formatted as one, and a year is not a quantity to be grouped. *@
        <p class="tmi-ink-copyright">
            @L["BrandCopyright", Clock.GetUtcNow().Year.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)]
        </p>
    </div>
</aside>
